      "diff": "@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@ wsbuglink:17779[]\n // * The Windows installers now ship with Qt 5.12.2.\n // They previously shipped with Qt 6.2.3.\n \n-If you upgraded to macOS 13 from an earlier version, you will likely have to open and run the “Uninstall ChmodBPF” package, then open and run “Install ChmodBPF” in order to reset the ChmodBPF Launch Daemon. wsbuglink:18734[].\n+If you’re running Wireshark on macOS and upgraded to macOS 13 from an earlier version, you will likely have to open and run the “Uninstall ChmodBPF” package, then open and run “Install ChmodBPF” in order to reset the ChmodBPF Launch Daemon. wsbuglink:18734[].\n \n === Bug Fixes\n \n@@ -44,8 +44,33 @@ The following bugs have been fixed:\n //* cveidlink:2014-2486[]\n //* Wireshark insists on subscribing to two dozen streaming services but only watches three.\n \n+* UTF-8 characters end up escaped in psml output. wsbuglink:10445[].\n+* DICOM Disscetion in reassembled PDV goes wrong. wsbuglink:13388[].\n+* \"Export Objects - IMF\" produces incorrect file, TCP reassembly fails with retransmissions that have additional data. wsbuglink:13523[].\n+* The intelligent scroll bar or minimap is not predictable on locating and scrolling. wsbuglink:13989[].\n+* If you mark (or unmark) the currently-selected frame, the packet details still say it's not marked (or it is marked) wsbuglink:14330[].\n+* An out-of-order packet incorrectly detected as retransmission breaks desegmentation of tcp stream. wsbuglink:15993[].\n+* Sorting Packet Loss Column is not sorting correct. wsbuglink:16785[].\n+* Some HTTPS packets cannot be decrypted. wsbuglink:17406[].\n+* SIP TCP decoding regression from Wireshark 1.99.0 to 3.6.8. wsbuglink:18411[].\n+* Frame comments not preserved when using filter to write new pcap from tshark. wsbuglink:18693[].\n+* ChmodBPF not working on macOS Ventura 13.1. wsbuglink:18734[].\n+* Wireshark GUI and window manager stuck after setting display filter. wsbuglink:18809[].\n+* Dissector bug, protocol H.261. wsbuglink:18812[].\n+* File extension heuristics are case-sensitive. wsbuglink:18821[].\n+* Symbolic links to packages in macOS dmg can't be double-clicked to install on macOS 13.2. wsbuglink:18830[].\n+* Potential memory leak in tshark.c. wsbuglink:18837[].\n+* ISO15765 and ISO10681 dissectors corrupt memory and Wireshark may crash. wsbuglink:18839[].\n+* Fuzz job crash output: fuzz-2023-02-05-7303.pcap. wsbuglink:18842[].\n+* f5fileinfo: Hardware platforms missing descriptions. wsbuglink:18848[].\n+* The lines in the intelligent scrollbar are off by one. wsbuglink:18850[].\n+* Wireshark crashes on invalid UDS packet in Lua context. wsbuglink:18865[].\n+* TECMP dissector shows the wrong Voltage in Vendor Data. wsbuglink:18871[].\n+* UDS: Names of RDTCI subfunctions 0x0b ... 0x0e are not correct. wsbuglink:18873[].\n+\n === New and Updated Features\n \n+There are no new or updated features in this release.\n \n === Removed Features and Support\n \n@@ -64,9 +89,37 @@ There are no new protocols in this release.\n === Updated Protocol Support\n \n // Add one protocol per line between the -- delimiters.\n-// ag -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v4.0.3.. | ag packet- | sort -u)\n+// ag -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v4.0.4.. | ag packet- | sort -u)\n [commaize]\n --\n+ASTERIX\n+BGP\n+DHCP\n+ERF\n+F5 Ethernet trailer\n+GMR-1 RR\n+Gryphon\n+GSM SMS\n+H.261\n+H.450\n+ISO 10681\n+ISO 15765\n+MIPv6\n+NAS-5gs\n+NR RRC\n+NS Trace\n+OptoMMP\n+PDCP-LTE\n+PDCP-NR\n+QSIG\n+ROHC\n+RSVP\n+RTCP\n+SIP\n+TCP\n+TECMP\n+TWAMP\n+UDS\n --\n \n === New and Updated Capture File Support\n",
